<%# The same register as the tag filter and the order, because it is the same
    kind of control: pick one of a handful. Carries the other two, as they
    carry it — three choices that have to survive each other.

    url_for without a controller keeps the index it is rendered on, so one
    partial serves both. %>
<%= render "shared/filter_row", name: "size", label: "Size",
      items: Sizing::SIZES.map { |key, label|
        [ label, url_for(size: key, q: params[:q], tag: params[:tag], sort: params[:sort]),
          size_key == key ]
      } %>
